Generator/subscribers\",\"subscription_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/Anil-matcha/AI-Youtube-Shorts-Generator/subscription\",\"svn_url\":\"https://github.com/Anil-matcha/AI-Youtube-Shorts-Generator\",\"tags_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/Anil-matcha/AI-Youtube-Shorts-Generator/tags\",\"teams_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/Anil-matcha/AI-Youtube-Shorts-Generator/teams\",\"temp_clone_token\":null,\"topics\":[\"2short-ai-alternative\",\"ai-clip-generator\",\"ai-clipping\",\"auto-clip\",\"auto-crop\",\"highlight-detection\",\"klap-alternative\",\"llm\",\"open-source\",\"opus-clip-alternative\",\"reels\",\"shorts-maker\",\"submagic-alternative\",\"tiktok\",\"vertical-video\",\"video-editing\",\"vidyo-ai-alternative\",\"viral-clips\",\"whisper\",\"youtube-shorts\"],\"trees_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/Anil-matcha/AI-Youtube-Shorts-Generator/git/trees{/sha}\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-08-01T12:43:22Z\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/Anil-matcha/AI-Youtube-Shorts-Generator\",\"visibility\":\"public\",\"watchers\":4447,\"watchers_count\":4447,\"web_commit_signoff_required\":false}},\"reason\":null,\"source_id\":\"github.hook-rubric\",\"status\":\"success\"},\"schema_version\":\"marketing.source-capture.v1\",\"source\":{\"adapter\":\"github_repo\",\"cadence\":\"daily\",\"enabled\":true,\"id\":\"github.hook-rubric\",\"languages\":[\"en\"],\"product_ids\":[\"aniccaios\",\"honne\",\"ebook-ja\",\"ebook-en\"],\"repo\":\"Anil-matcha/AI-Youtube-Shorts-Generator\"}}}\n{\"file\":\"/Users/anicca/anicca/skills/earn/marketing-engine/evidence/intel/pulls/68f5220fe826411ab0d41408bda1f09e/github.kdp-scout.json\",\"keys\":[\"result\",\"schema_version\",\"source\"],\"item\":{\"result\":{\"api_status\":null,\"cache\":{},\"canonical_url\":\"https://github.com/rxpelle/kdp-scout\",\"error_class\":null,\"http_status\":200,\"item_ids\":[\"github:rxpelle/kdp-scout@92131151378f83142ac214ed2eca7474c405efee\"],\"payload\":{\"latest_commit\":{\"author\":{\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/258741235?v=4\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/nanookclaw/events{/privacy}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/nanookclaw/followers\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/nanookclaw/following{/other_user}\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/nanookclaw/gists{/gist_id}\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/nanookclaw\",\"id\":258741235,\"login\":\"nanookclaw\",\"node_id\":\"U_kgDOD2wT8w\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/nanookclaw/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/nanookclaw/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/nanookclaw/repos\",\"site_admin\":false,\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/nanookclaw/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/nanookclaw/subscriptions\",\"type\":\"User\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/nanookclaw\",\"user_view_type\":\"public\"},\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/rxpelle/kdp-scout/commits/92131151378f83142ac214ed2eca7474c405efee/comments\",\"commit\":{\"author\":{\"date\":\"2026-06-05T23:28:08Z\",\"email\":\"nanook@agentmail.to\",\"name\":\"nanookclaw\"},\"comment_count\":0,\"committer\":{\"date\":\"2026-06-05T23:28:08Z\",\"email\":\"noreply@github.com\",\"name\":\"GitHub\"},\"message\":\"feat: add output option for reports and exports (#8)\\n\\n* feat: add output option for reports and exports\\n\\n* test: add real-engine integration tests for output file capture\\n\\nThe existing CLI output tests mock ReportingEngine and emit via the\\nbuiltin print(), so they never exercise the actual Rich console\\nrendering that --output relies on (contextlib.redirect_stdout capturing\\nrich.console.Console). Add two tests that run the real engine against a\\nseeded temp database and assert the rendered Rich table lands in the\\nfile, plus the empty-DB zero-row boundary.\\n\\nAlso fix the existing mock-based tests, which assumed Click >=8.2's\\nalways-separate stderr and failed under the project's pinned Click\\n8.1.8. A make_runner() helper requests mix_stderr=False on 8.1.x and\\nfalls back to the default runner on 8.2+, keeping the suite green on\\nboth.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Nanook <nanookclaw@users.noreply.github.com>\\nCo-authored-by: Randy Pellegrini <rxpelle@users.noreply.github.com>\\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"tree\":{\"sha\":\"387cb3b8a67a75f6f86320b4b0b58f80765aeb87\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/rxpelle/kdp-scout/git/trees/387cb3b8a67a75f6f86320b4b0b58f80765aeb87\"},\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/rxpelle/kdp-scout/git/commits/92131151378f83142ac214ed2eca7474c405efee\",\"verification\":{\"payload\":\"tree 387cb3b8a67a75f6f86320b4b0b58f80765aeb87\\nparent 61c320fbd85dcfcb633cb1526294392c621de3af\\nauthor nanookclaw <nanook@agentmail.to> 1780702088 +0000\\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780702088 -0700\\n\\nfeat: add output option for reports and exports (#8)\\n\\n* feat: add output option for reports and exports\\n\\n* test: add real-engine integration tests for output file capture\\n\\nThe existing CLI output tests mock ReportingEngine and emit via the\\nbuiltin print(), so they never exercise the actual Rich console\\nrendering that --output relies on (contextlib.redirect_stdout capturing\\nrich.console.Console). Add two tests that run the real engine against a\\nseeded temp database and assert the rendered Rich table lands in the\\nfile, plus the empty-DB zero-row boundary.\\n\\nAlso fix the existing mock-based tests, which assumed Click >=8.2's\\nalways-separate stderr and failed under the project's pinned Click\\n8.1.8. A make_runner() helper requests mix_stderr=False on 8.1.x and\\nfalls back to the default runner on 8.2+, keeping the suite green on\\nboth.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\